WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.800
Will the Skywalker Saga end by finally putting
to rest questions over a certain character's

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:06.640
parentage?

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.440
According to some fresh rumors posted on the
fan site Making Star Wars, there's a chance

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.300
that The Rise of Skywalker will do just that.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.560
Warning: These are unsubstantiated rumors
attributed to anonymous sources, so take them

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.020
with a grain of salt, perhaps washed down
with some green milk.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.820
In other words: potential spoilers ahead!

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:31.420
Making Star Wars editor-in-chief Jason Ward
claims that The Rise of Skywalker takes audiences

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.530
to an Endor-like tree-covered planet immediately
after the opening crawl.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:42.190
There, it's said that a pair of Jedi wearing
white helmets are seen dueling, a green lightsaber

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.700
against a blue lightsaber.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:48.739
It's then revealed that the two Jedi are Luke
and Leia, appearing as the younger versions

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.640
of themselves as seen in Return of the Jedi.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.559
Rumor has it that this flashback sequence
not only demonstrates how Leia was able to

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:01.449
summon the Force and save herself from certain
death in space in The Last Jedi, but also

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:07.430
sets up a plot in which Leia trains Rey throughout
The Rise of Skywalker, which leads Rey to

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:12.880
make an important decision following a major
revelation: she's a member of the Palpatine

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:13.880
family.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.160
Yep: rumor has it that Rey is a descendant
of Emperor Palpatine, the villain otherwise

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:24.270
known as Darth Sidious who destroyed the Jedi
Order, led the Galactic Empire, and was a

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.020
mentor to Darth Vader.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.250
Apparently, Rey discovers she's a Palpatine
and decides to reject her parentage, renaming

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:36.420
herself as a Skywalker at the end of the film,
thus explaining why the movie is titled The

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.160
Rise of Skywalker.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.940
As far as rumors go, this one doesn't set
off a whole lot of alarms.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.920
Rey's parentage has always been a point of
contention amongst fans, most of whom aren't

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.680
satisfied with the idea presented by Kylo
Ren in The Last Jedi: that Rey's mother and

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.380
father were nobodies, and alcoholics, to boot.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.900
The Last Jedi writer-director Rian Johnson
has said that the mystery of Rey's parentage

00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:03.960
hasn't been entirely resolved, revealing in
January 2018 that "anything's still open"

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.660
since he isn't involved with The Rise of Skywalker.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:13.320
It was reported in April 2018 that J.J. Abrams,
who wrote and directed The Force Awakens and

00:02:13.329 --> 00:02:18.260
The Rise of Skywalker, actually had a different
plan for Rey's identity than the one presented

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.480
in The Last Jedi.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:25.020
Simon Pegg, the actor behind the Jakku junk
boss Unkar Plutt, said during an appearance

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:30.610
on the Happy Sad Confused podcast that what
Abrams had intended to eventually reveal about

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:35.560
Rey's parents was, quote, "undone slightly"
by The Last Jedi.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.940
He added that there was talk of Rey having
a "relevant lineage" rather than being the

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.810
child of two alcoholic traders from Jakku.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:48.099
Daisy Ridley herself has mentioned that Palpatine
plays a pivotal role in the upcoming movie,

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:53.469
going so far as to say that the infamous baddie
is, quote, "very instrumental to the plot

00:02:53.469 --> 00:02:56.880
of the film" and that there's an important
reason for his return.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.400
She told IGN in August 2019,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.780
"It's not just like he appears again; it's
all explained."

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:09.200
Could The Rise of Skywalker explain that Palpatine
returned to lure his kin to the dark side

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:13.560
of the Force, leaving the Resistance that
much more vulnerable and the First Order that

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.860
much more powerful?

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.840
Maybe!

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.860
After all, it could help shed light on why
recent footage from The Rise of Skywalker

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.120
showed Rey wearing a dark robe and wielding
a double-bladed red lightsaber.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:29.480
Perhaps Rey gets entangled in a moral quandary,
pulling away from the light side and potentially

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.320
considering converting to the dark side when
possible temptation proves too strong.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.280
This is far from the first "Rey is a Palpatine"
rumor we've heard over the years.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:43.480
Fans have been speculating for quite some
time now that Rey is connected to Emperor

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:49.279
Palpatine, with some even believing that Rey
is technically both a Skywalker and a Palpatine,

00:03:49.279 --> 00:03:54.459
with the idea that Palpatine made Rey as a
clone of Luke from the hand he lost in The

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.120
Empire Strikes Back.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:01.240
It's a wild theory for sure, but it could
explain why Emperor Palpatine returns in The

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:06.580
Rise of Skywalker: to retrieve the stolen
clone and bring her to the dark side.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.780
There's also a pretty good chance that this
rumor isn't anything of consequence, and that

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:16.690
what actually ends up happening in The Rise
of Skywalker is nothing that anyone has theorized

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:17.600
thus far.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:23.880
Perhaps the Skywalker who rises in the upcoming
film isn't Rey or even a single person, but

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:28.200
a new generation of Force users now known
as Skywalkers.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.500
We won't know for sure until, well, we know
for sure, when The Rise of Skywalker reveals

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.280
all on December 20th.

